{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q108321170","formula":"C₁₃H₂₀FNO₂S","hill":"C13H20FNO2S","elements":["H","C","N","O","F","S"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"F":1.0,"H":20.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"2C-T-28"},"descriptions":{"en":"2C-T-28, also known as 4-(3-fluoropropylthio)-2,5-dimethoxyphenethylamine or as 2C-T-FP, is a psychedelic drug related to 2C-T-7 and 2C-T-21. It was named by Alexander Shulgin but was never made or tested by him, and was instead first synthesised by Daniel Trachsel some years later. It has a binding affinity of 75 nM at 5-HT2A and 28 nM at 5-HT2C. It is reportedly a potent psychedelic drug with an active dose in the 8–20 mg range, and a duration of action of 8–10 hours, with prominent visual effects."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":12063262,"mass":273.37,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=CC(=C(C=C1CCN)OC)SCCCF","inchikey":"XAFVGDRNPGLCMI-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-[4-(3-fluoropropylsulfanyl)-2,5-dimethoxyphenyl]ethanamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"12063262","atoms":38,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.305,"y":-0.048,"z":1.182,"el":"S"},{"x":5.789,"y":-0.399,"z":-0.171,"el":"F"},{"x":-2.23,"y":-2.164,"z":0.104,"el":"O"},{"x":0.887,"y":2.385,"z":-0.013,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.734,"y":0.655,"z":-0.411,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.969,"y":0.155,"z":-0.443,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.362,"y":0.227,"z":-0.973,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.463,"y":-1.038,"z":0.073,"el":"C"},{"x":0.64,"y":0.055,"z":0.542,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.17,"y":1.298,"z":-0.466,"el":"C"},{"x":0.134,"y":1.248,"z":0.026,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.159,"y":-1.088,"z":0.565,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.374,"y":0.613,"z":0.115,"el":"C"},{"x":3.031,"y":-1.316,"z":0.106,"el":"C"},{"x":3.678,"y":-0.731,"z":-1.149,"el":"C"},{"x":4.811,"y":0.244,"z":-0.862,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.634,"y":-3.34,"z":0.648,"el":"C"},{"x":0.82,"y":3.243,"z":1.124,